<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Northern Yuan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Northern Yuan was the regime maintained by the Mongol imperial line on the Mongolian steppe after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. The last Yuan emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toghon-temur">Toghon Temur</a>, fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a> in 1368 as Ming forces approached. His successors continued to claim the Yuan title in a diminished form, and accounts of the Yuan Dynasty date its continued existence to the early fifteenth century.</p></div>
